From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Minimal <noreply@minimal.dev>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gvproxy: no route from the virtual network to the host's
 loopback

A configuration that names no NAT entry gets one from upstream: the host
address, by default the last usable address of the subnet, is translated to
127.0.0.1, and the gateway answers ARP for it. Anything that can put a frame
on the virtual network then reaches every TCP and UDP port on the host's
loopback. An empty map in the YAML does not switch the default off.

Minimal gives boxes a named set of host loopback ports through its own
relay and wants no other way there.

Remove both defaults, so a NAT entry and a virtual address of the gateway
exist only when the configuration names them.

The TCP, UDP and ICMP forwarders refuse a destination that a dial from this
process takes to the host itself, after NAT translation: a loopback address
and the unspecified address, which connect(2) reads as this host. A UDP
datagram to 0.0.0.0 arrived at a listener on the host's loopback before
this change.

Every changed file carries a notice that it was modified, as section 4(b)
of the Apache License 2.0 asks.

Applies to containers/gvisor-tap-vsock v0.9.0
(6dbb5d4fa0033356c72a201346f8350594229868) after patch 0001.
---
